<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 1: </span>Performance evaluation on the <span id="Sx4.T1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">LibriSpeech test-clean</span> across different audio prompt lengths. <span id="Sx4.T1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Bold</span> indicates the best result, and <span id="Sx4.T1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_underline">underline</span> indicates the second-best result. (<math id="Sx4.T1.m36" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\uparrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">↑</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\uparrow</annotation></semantics></math>) indicates that higher values are better, while (<math id="Sx4.T1.m37" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\downarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">↓</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\downarrow</annotation></semantics></math>) indicates that lower values are better. <math id="Sx4.T1.m38" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[\varheartsuit]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mtext class="undefined">\varheartsuit</mtext><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[\varheartsuit]</annotation></semantics></math> means reproduced results. <math id="Sx4.T1.m39" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[\vardiamondsuit]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mtext class="undefined">\vardiamondsuit</mtext><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[\vardiamondsuit]</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Sx4.T1.m40" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[\spadesuit]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">♠</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[\spadesuit]</annotation></semantics></math> mean results inferred from official and ufficial checkpoints, respectively. Abbreviation: VB (VoxBox), LT (LibriTTS), GS (GigaSpeech).</figcaption>
</figure>
