<section id="Sx6" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section">Implementation Details</h2>

<div id="Sx6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Algorithm <a href="#alg1" title="Algorithm 1 ‣ Implementation Details ‣ Flamed-TTS: Flow Matching Attention-Free Models for Efficient Generating and Dynamic Pacing Zero-shot Text-to-Speech" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> outlines the method for generating and expanding phoneme durations, including the insertion of silences after each phoneme.</p>
</div>
<figure id="alg1" class="ltx_float ltx_float_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="alg1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 1</span> </span> <span id="alg1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Duration &amp; Silent Phoneme Generator</span> Sampling and Expanding Algorithm</figcaption>
<p id="alg1.5" class="ltx_p ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom"><span id="alg1.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Input</span>: The encoded phonemes <math id="alg1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbf{p}_{1:L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐩</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{p}_{1:L}</annotation></semantics></math> of the length <math id="alg1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math>, and the first token of <math id="alg1.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbf{p}_{1:L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐩</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{p}_{1:L}</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="alg1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\verb|[SIL]|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace" mathvariant="monospace">[SIL]</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\verb|[SIL]|</annotation></semantics></math>, the number of sampling step <math id="alg1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math>, and step size <math id="alg1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta t=\frac{1}{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta t=\frac{1}{N}</annotation></semantics></math>.
<br class="ltx_break"><span id="alg1.5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Output</span>: Expanded encoded phoneme sequence <math id="alg1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{p}_{\mathbf{expand}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐩</mi><mi>𝐞𝐱𝐩𝐚𝐧𝐝</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{p}_{\mathbf{expand}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
<br class="ltx_break ltx_break">
<div id="alg1.6" class="ltx_listing ltx_listing">
<div id="alg1.l1" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">1:</span>
            
          Sample <math id="alg1.l1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{d}_{0}\sim\mathcal{N}(0,I),\mathbf{d}_{t}\in\mathcal{R}^{L\times 1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐝</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐝</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{d}_{0}\sim\mathcal{N}(0,I),\mathbf{d}_{t}\in\mathcal{R}^{L\times 1}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l2" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">2:</span>
            
          Sample <math id="alg1.l2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{s}_{0}\sim\mathcal{N}(0,I),\mathbf{s}_{t}\in\mathcal{R}^{L\times 1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐬</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐬</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{s}_{0}\sim\mathcal{N}(0,I),\mathbf{s}_{t}\in\mathcal{R}^{L\times 1}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l3" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">3:</span>
            
          <span id="alg1.l3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> <math id="alg1.l3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=0</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">to</span> <math id="alg1.l3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\Delta_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\Delta_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">with step</span> <math id="alg1.l3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta t</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l3.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l4" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">4:</span>
            
            <math id="alg1.l4.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbf{d}_{t+1}\leftarrow\mathbf{d}_{t}+\Delta t\cdot\mathcal{D}_{\phi}(\mathbf{d}_{t},\mathbf{p}_{1:L},t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐝</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><msub><mi>𝐝</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐝</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐩</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{d}_{t+1}\leftarrow\mathbf{d}_{t}+\Delta t\cdot\mathcal{D}_{\phi}(\mathbf{d}_{t},\mathbf{p}_{1:L},t)</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l5" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">5:</span>
            
            <math id="alg1.l5.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbf{s}_{t+1}\leftarrow\mathbf{s}_{t}+\Delta t\cdot\mathcal{S}_{\xi}(\mathbf{s}_{t},\mathbf{p}_{1:L},t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐬</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><msub><mi>𝐬</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>ξ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐬</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐩</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{s}_{t+1}\leftarrow\mathbf{s}_{t}+\Delta t\cdot\mathcal{S}_{\xi}(\mathbf{s}_{t},\mathbf{p}_{1:L},t)</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l6" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">6:</span>
            
          <span id="alg1.l6.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg1.l6.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l7" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">7:</span>
            
          <math id="alg1.l7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{p}_{\mathbf{expand}}\leftarrow\{\varnothing\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐩</mi><mi>𝐞𝐱𝐩𝐚𝐧𝐝</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{p}_{\mathbf{expand}}\leftarrow\{\varnothing\}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l8" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">8:</span>
            
          <math id="alg1.l8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="sil\leftarrow\mathbf{p}_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><msub><mi>𝐩</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">sil\leftarrow\mathbf{p}_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l9" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">9:</span>
            
          <span id="alg1.l9.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> <math id="alg1.l9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\quad\mathbf{in}\quad 1\dots L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mi>𝐢𝐧</mi><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\quad\mathbf{in}\quad 1\dots L</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l9.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l10" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">10:</span>
            
            <span id="alg1.l10.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">if</span> <math id="alg1.l10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i=1</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l10.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">then</span>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l11" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">11:</span>
            
             <math id="alg1.l11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="||d_{i}||=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">||d_{i}||=0</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l12" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">12:</span>
            
            <span id="alg1.l12.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">else</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l13" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">13:</span>
            
             <math id="alg1.l13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="||d_{i}||=\max(\left\lfloor\exp{\mathbf{d}_{1,i}}\right\rceil,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>⌊</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>𝐝</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>⌉</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">||d_{i}||=\max(\left\lfloor\exp{\mathbf{d}_{1,i}}\right\rceil,1)</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l14" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">14:</span>
            
            <span id="alg1.l14.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg1.l14.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">if</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l15" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">15:</span>
            
            <math id="alg1.l15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="||s_{i}||=\left\lfloor\exp{\mathbf{s}_{1,i}}\right\rceil" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>⌊</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>𝐬</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>⌉</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">||s_{i}||=\left\lfloor\exp{\mathbf{s}_{1,i}}\right\rceil</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l16" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">16:</span>
            
            <math id="alg1.l16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{p}_{\mathbf{expand}}\leftarrow\mathbf{p}_{\mathbf{expand}}+\{p_{i}\dots p_{i}\}_{||d_{i}||}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐩</mi><mi>𝐞𝐱𝐩𝐚𝐧𝐝</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐩</mi><mi>𝐞𝐱𝐩𝐚𝐧𝐝</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{p}_{\mathbf{expand}}\leftarrow\mathbf{p}_{\mathbf{expand}}+\{p_{i}\dots p_{i}\}_{||d_{i}||}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l17" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">17:</span>
            
            <math id="alg1.l17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{p}_{\mathbf{expand}}\leftarrow\mathbf{p}_{\mathbf{expand}}+\{sil\dots sil\}_{||s_{i}||}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐩</mi><mi>𝐞𝐱𝐩𝐚𝐧𝐝</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐩</mi><mi>𝐞𝐱𝐩𝐚𝐧𝐝</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{p}_{\mathbf{expand}}\leftarrow\mathbf{p}_{\mathbf{expand}}+\{sil\dots sil\}_{||s_{i}||}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l18" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">18:</span>
            
          <span id="alg1.l18.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg1.l18.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span>
</div>
</div>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="Sx7" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section">Experiment Details</h2>

<section id="Sx7.SSx1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection">Metrics</h3>

<div id="Sx7.SSx1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<ul id="Sx7.I3" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="Sx7.I3.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="Sx7.I3.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx7.I3.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Sx7.I3.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Real-Time Factor (RTF)</span>: A key measure of system efficiency, especially for real-time applications, RTF indicates the time needed to generate one second of speech. We evaluate RTF for all models in a complete end-to-end setup on an NVIDIA 80GB A100 GPU.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="Sx7.I3.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="Sx7.I3.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx7.I3.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Sx7.I3.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Number of Function Evaluations (NFE)</span>: This metric counts how many times the model’s guiding function (e.g., score or drift function) is calculated during sampling. It’s particularly relevant when the generative process involves solving an ordinary differential equation (ODE), as in score-based generative models using the probability flow ODE method.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="Sx7.I3.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="Sx7.I3.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx7.I3.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Sx7.I3.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">UTMOS</span>: A deep learning-based tool for evaluating speech quality by predicting mean opinion scores (MOS). It replaces expensive and time-intensive subjective evaluations, offering predictions that closely match human judgments.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="Sx7.I3.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="Sx7.I3.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx7.I3.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Sx7.I3.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">SIM-O and SIM-R</span> : These metrics measure speaker similarity. SIM-O compares synthesized speech to the original prompt, while SIM-R compares it to a reconstructed prompt from FACodec. Both are calculated using cosine similarity of speaker embeddings extracted via WavLM-TDCNN, with values ranging from -1 to 1 (higher values indicate greater similarity).</p>
</div></li>
<li id="Sx7.I3.i5" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="Sx7.I3.i5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx7.I3.i5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Sx7.I3.i5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Word Error Rate (WER)</span>: This evaluates the accuracy of word pronunciation in speech synthesis systems. We use a CTC-based HuBERT model, pre-trained on LibriLight and fine-tuned on LibriSpeech’s 960-hour dataset, to transcribe generated speech and compare it to the text prompt.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="Sx7.I3.i6" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="Sx7.I3.i6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx7.I3.i6.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Sx7.I3.i6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Acoustic Accuracy &amp; Error (<math id="Sx7.I3.i6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{F0}_{\mathbf{ACC}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐅𝟎</mi><mi>𝐀𝐂𝐂</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{F0}_{\mathbf{ACC}}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="Sx7.I3.i6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{F0}_{\mathbf{RMSE}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐅𝟎</mi><mi>𝐑𝐌𝐒𝐄</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{F0}_{\mathbf{RMSE}}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="Sx7.I3.i6.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{EN}_{\mathbf{ACC}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐄𝐍</mi><mi>𝐀𝐂𝐂</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{EN}_{\mathbf{ACC}}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="Sx7.I3.i6.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{EN}_{\mathbf{RMSE}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐄𝐍</mi><mi>𝐑𝐌𝐒𝐄</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{EN}_{\mathbf{RMSE}}</annotation></semantics></math>)</span>: These assess how well synthesized speech aligns with the audio prompt, focusing on pitch (<math id="Sx7.I3.i6.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{F0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐅𝟎</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{F0}</annotation></semantics></math>) and energy (<math id="Sx7.I3.i6.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{EN}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐄𝐍</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{EN}</annotation></semantics></math>). Accuracy is measured by categorizing F0 and energy into high, normal, and low levels, following methods from PromptTTS and TextrolSpeech. Additionally, Root Mean Square Error (RMSE) quantifies differences in F0 and energy between synthesized speech and prompts.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="Sx7.I3.i7" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="Sx7.I3.i7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx7.I3.i7.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Sx7.I3.i7.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Speech Rate</span>: This metric quantifies how quickly the synthesized speech is delivered. It is computed as the ratio between the total duration of the synthesized waveform and the number of syllables in the reference sentence.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="Sx7.I3.i8" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="Sx7.I3.i8.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx7.I3.i8.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Sx7.I3.i8.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Mean Phoneme Duration (MPhD)</span>: This metric evaluates the average duration of phonemes within a sentence. It is computed by averaging the durations of all spoken phonemes, excluding silences. Phoneme boundaries and their corresponding durations are obtained using the Montreal Forced Aligner (MFA) toolkit <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib21" title="" class="ltx_ref">McAuliffe et al. 2017</a>)</cite>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="Sx7.I3.i9" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="Sx7.I3.i9.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx7.I3.i9.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Sx7.I3.i9.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Number of Pauses (#Pauses)</span>: This metric evaluates the average number of silent segments in a sentence, calculated by taking the mean of the counts of silent segments.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="Sx7.I3.i10" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="Sx7.I3.i10.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx7.I3.i10.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Sx7.I3.i10.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Mean Pause Duration (MPaD)</span>: This metric evaluates the average duration of silences within a sentence. It is computed by averaging the durations of all silent segments. Similar to <span id="Sx7.I3.i10.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">MPhD</span>, the alignments of silences and the corresponding durations are extracted using MFA toolkit.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</section>
<section id="Sx7.SSx2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection">Baselines</h3>

<div id="Sx7.SSx2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx7.SSx2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We benchmark our model against several state-of-the-art zero-shot TTS systems, using publicly available implementations and pre-trained checkpoints where applicable:</p>
</div>
<div id="Sx7.SSx2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<ul id="Sx7.I4" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="Sx7.I4.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="Sx7.I4.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx7.I4.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Sx7.I4.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">VALL-E</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib3" title="" class="ltx_ref">Chen et al. 2025</a>)</cite>: We reproduce VALL-E using the Amphion framework <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib41" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhang et al. 2024a</a>)</cite>, training it on the LibriTTS dataset with the same configuration as our proposed model to ensure a fair and controlled comparison. This baseline relies on SpeechTokenizer <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib42" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhang et al. 2024b</a>)</cite> as the speech tokenizer.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="Sx7.I4.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="Sx7.I4.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx7.I4.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Sx7.I4.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">NaturalSpeech 2</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib31" title="" class="ltx_ref">Shen et al. 2024</a>)</cite>: We employ the Amphion toolkit <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib41" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhang et al. 2024a</a>)</cite> along with its corresponding pre-trained checkpoint<span id="footnote2" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">2</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">2</sup>
                    <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note">2</span>
                    
                    
                  <span class="ltx_ref ltx_nolink ltx_url ltx_ref_self">https://huggingface.co/amphion/naturalspeech2˙libritts/tree/main/checkpoint</span></span></span></span>, trained on the LibriTTS dataset <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib40" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zen et al. 2019</a>)</cite>. This baseline relies on Encodec <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib5" title="" class="ltx_ref">Défossez et al. 2023</a>)</cite> as the speech tokenizer.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="Sx7.I4.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="Sx7.I4.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx7.I4.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Sx7.I4.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">VoiceCraft</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib29" title="" class="ltx_ref">Peng et al. 2024</a>)</cite>: We adopt the official implementation and utilize the pre-trained model checkpoint<span id="footnote3" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">3</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">3</sup>
                    <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note">3</span>
                    
                    
                  <span class="ltx_ref ltx_nolink ltx_url ltx_ref_self">https://huggingface.co/pyp1/VoiceCraft/blob/main/830M˙TTSEnhanced.pth</span></span></span></span>, trained on the GigaSpeech corpus <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib1" title="" class="ltx_ref">Chen et al. 2021</a>)</cite>. This baseline relies on Encodec as the speech tokenizer.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="Sx7.I4.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="Sx7.I4.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx7.I4.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Sx7.I4.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">F5-TTS</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib4" title="" class="ltx_ref">Chen et al. 2024b</a>)</cite>: We utilize the official implementation<span id="footnote4" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">4</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">4</sup>
                    <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note">4</span>
                    
                    
                  <span class="ltx_ref ltx_nolink ltx_url ltx_ref_self">https://github.com/SWivid/F5-TTS</span></span></span></span> and reproduce the model on the LibriTTS dataset <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib40" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zen et al. 2019</a>)</cite> following the original training configurations.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="Sx7.I4.i5" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="Sx7.I4.i5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx7.I4.i5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Sx7.I4.i5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Spark-TTS</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib34" title="" class="ltx_ref">Wang et al. 2025</a>)</cite>: We utilize the official implementation <span id="footnote5" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">5</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">5</sup>
                    <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note">5</span>
                    
                    
                  <span class="ltx_ref ltx_nolink ltx_url ltx_ref_self">https://github.com/SparkAudio/Spark-TTS</span></span></span></span> and official checkpoint <span id="footnote6" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">6</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">6</sup>
                    <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note">6</span>
                    
                    
                  <span class="ltx_ref ltx_nolink ltx_url ltx_ref_self">https://huggingface.co/SparkAudio/Spark-TTS-0.5B</span></span></span></span> trained on the VoxBox corpus, which was also introduced in the same paper of Spark-TTS. This baseline relies on BiCodec <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib34" title="" class="ltx_ref">Wang et al. 2025</a>)</cite> as the speech tokenizer.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="Sx7.I4.i6" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="Sx7.I4.i6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx7.I4.i6.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Sx7.I4.i6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">OZSpeech</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib9" title="" class="ltx_ref">Huynh-Nguyen et al. 2025</a>)</cite>: We laverage the official repository and checkpoint <span id="footnote7" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">7</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">7</sup>
                    <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note">7</span>
                    
                    
                  <span class="ltx_ref ltx_nolink ltx_url ltx_ref_self">https://github.com/ozspeech/OZSpeech</span></span></span></span> trained on the LibriTTS corpus. This baseline relies on FACodec <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib11" title="" class="ltx_ref">Ju et al. 2024</a>)</cite> as the speech tokenizer.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</section>
</section>
